    "findingId": "F5",
    "verdict": "true-positive",
    "adjustedSeverity": "BUG",
    "reasoning": "The missing control is real and verified end-to-end. The page declares no `rateLimit` and packages/site/src/index.ts passes none to `Mochi.serve()`, so `buildLimiter(undefined, pattern)` returns null (Mochi.ts:801-828) and `checkRouteLimit` (Mochi.ts:981) is a no-op; I confirmed `wrapRequest` wraps the POST action handler too (Mochi.ts:1026-1027), so a page-level `rateLimit` with `skip: (req) => req.method !== 'POST'` would in fact gate these actions — exactly the idiom already applied to `/demos/queue` and `/demos/reload-form-data` (both `limit: 60, window: '1m'`) by commit 1289d8f8, plus 60/m on captcha mint and 120/m on `/og`. So this is a clean, inconsistent gap in a control the maintainers demonstrably treat as required. The per-request work is as described: `sendEmail` → `renderEmailComponent` does a `renderStatic` SSR render, joins scoped CSS, runs `@css-inline/css-inline-wasm` `inline()`, then an `HTMLRewriter` pass and `htmlToText` (email/render.ts, mailer.ts:89-95); `sendPhoto` re-reads the JPEG from disk every request (routes.ts:26) and the bytes are retained in the outbox entry (devOutbox.ts:70-74). I also confirmed the deployed site really is in dev mode — Dockerfile's ENTRYPOINT is `bun run dev:${WORKSPACE}` and packages/site's `dev` script sets `NODE_ENV=development` — so the transport is `dev` (email/config.ts:12), the capture target is the shared process-global outbox capped at `MAX_OUTBOX = 100`, and CSRF only warns in development, making the POST reachable with no Origin at all. I am downgrading from MEDIUM because the amplification is modest rather than asymmetric: every ordinary page on this site is an unlimited unauthenticated SSR render, so the marginal cost here is roughly a CSS-inline pass and a page-cached 32 KB read; no mail is ever delivered (recipient, subject, body and attachment are all fixed server-side and the transport never sends); and the one distinctive effect, evicting other visitors' captures from the bounded dev outbox, degrades only a dev-only viewer. Real defect, correct fix, non-security-grade impact."
